 *
 * Stands in for the GPU service behind the exact §6b contract, so Rung 3 is a
 * single URL change in the main workflow's "Start CV job" node.
 *
 * It is an n8n workflow rather than a local FastAPI app because n8n Cloud
 * cannot reach localhost, and a tunnel is one more thing that can die mid-demo.
 *
 * This node builds the whole §6b payload up front and parks it in workflow
 * static data. /cv-mock/result then serves "processing" on the first poll and
 * "done" from the second, which is what makes the polling loop in the main
 * workflow genuinely loop instead of short-circuiting on the first call.
